      "section": "Marker genes and pathways",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Left, marker genes against cell clusters: dot size is the fraction of cells expressing the gene, colour its mean expression, so a marker is a large bright dot alone in its column (nf-core/scrnaseq counts after clustering). Right, the same marks on an enrichment table: one row per pathway, x the normalised enrichment score, size the gene-set size, colour the adjusted p-value (GSEA or g:Profiler output of nf-core/differentialabundance). Colour and sort controls sit in each tile header.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
